 carry on with the other products. It doesn't say whether hardship does, so I kept Brief A's behaviour of ending the call.\n- **Incomplete dates:** neither brief says how to read a promise date given without a month or year, such as \"the 15th\".\n\n**One judgement call to check:** I kept `ask_once_first: true` for refusing to talk. The brief says to close when the customer \"says twice\" they don't want to talk, so the first refusal is not acted on. The field is described as \"ask once whether you can help\", which the brief doesn't say for this case."}
{"event": "policy_compiled", "run_id": "2f536912ab9e4fcba8a66b6c8d9ee419", "pid": 18127, "time": "2026-10-10T15:12:37-0700", "elapsed_s": 185.515, "artifact": "out/rehearsal-ab.policy.json", "bands": 2, "identity_fields": ["date_of_birth", "phone_last4"], "special_cases": ["already_paid", "dispute", "hardship", "restructuring", "human", "scam", "refuse_to_talk", "robot", "cannot_answer", "change_recorded_promise"], "unresolved": [{"topic": "hardship with several products", "text": "Brief B lists `hardship` as an add_note reason but, unlike dispute and already paid (rule 9), does not say whether a hardship mention on one product continues with the other products; kept Brief A behaviour (offer support transfer, no notes on transfer; if declined, note unpromised products and close no_promise / hardship, unless a promise was recorded).", "doc": "sources/001-brief-b.md"}, {"topic": "missing date parts", "text": "The documents do not say how to interpret a promise date given without a month or year (e.g. \"the 15th\").", "doc": "sources/000-brief-a.md"}, {"topic": "promise write failure sentence", "text": "Rule 37 requires saying that the promise could not be recorded after a second create_promise failure; the IR has no phrase field for it, the words are not dictated (content only: say you could not record it).", "doc": "sources/000-brief-a.md"}, {"topic": "no other terms", "text": "Rule 33: never offer a discount, a waiver, an instalment plan or any term not in the brief. No IR field; must be enforced in the prompt text.", "doc": "sources/000-brief-a.md"}, {"topic": "relatives", "text": "Rule 10: a relative may not answer the security questions and may not be told anything about the account, even if they offer to pay. No dedicated IR field beyond the third-party flow; must be enforced in the prompt text.", "doc": "sources/000-brief-a.md"}], "audit_fixed": ["phrases.opening: replaced 'this is Freya Bank's digital assistant calling from Freya Bank' (redundant, and 'Freya Bank's digital assistant' is the robot reply wording) with a sentence carrying exactly the rule 1 content: a digital assistant calling from Freya Bank, call recorded. opening_verbatim stays false.", "phrases.prohibited_before_verification: added the product names 'credit card', 'personal loan', 'car loan' because rule 1 forbids saying 'the product' before verification; removed the corresponding unresolved entry.", "unresolved: added entries for rule 33 (no other terms), rule 10 (relatives) and the rule 37 failure sentence, which have no IR field.", "Source spans enriched (identity unclear/asking-purpose, amounts full-first/accept range, human before/after verification, transfer-after-promise, all_today_question origin in Brief B rule 4)."], "audit_unresolved": ["Whether a hardship mention on one product ends the call or continues with other products in Brief B (Brief B rule 9 names only dispute and already paid); kept Brief A closing behaviour.", "How to read a promise date given without month or year.", "Words for the 'could not record' sentence after two create_promise failures (content only, no IR field).", "Rule 33 and rule 10 constraints have no IR field and must be carried by prompt text."]}
